From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: rock-2a: run the SD card at 50 MHz

On the ROCK 2F, UHS SDR104 at 150 MHz fails every read from the SD card.
The ROCK 2A uses the same SD circuit. Use high speed at 50 MHz, as the
mainline kernels do.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-rock-2a.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-rock-2a.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-rock-2a.dts	2026-10-23 08:36:05.148429101 +0000
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-rock-2a.dts	2026-10-23 08:36:05.164429256 +0000
@@ -402,15 +402,12 @@
 	cap-mmc-highspeed;
 	cap-sd-highspeed;
 	disable-wp;
-	max-frequency = <150000000>;
+	/* UHS SDR104 at 150 MHz fails every read: use high speed at 50 MHz */
+	max-frequency = <50000000>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&sdmmc_clk &sdmmc_cmd &sdmmc_det &sdmmc_bus4>;
 	rockchip,default-sample-phase = <90>;
 	supports-sd;
-	sd-uhs-sdr12;
-	sd-uhs-sdr25;
-	sd-uhs-sdr50;
-	sd-uhs-sdr104;
 	vqmmc-supply = <&vccio_sd>;
 	vmmc-supply = <&vcc_sd>;
 	status = "okay";
